# groups -- groups of books for EBaC's searches: "=nt" is every verse of
# the group nt (EBaC 2.2). See "Groups of books" in readme.architecture.
#
# One group to a line: its name, then its members, which are taken in
# order, starting from no books:
#
#   rom        a book, written as after "@" (enough of its name to be
#              unique; a number may stand for a Roman numeral: 1co)
#   rom..phil  the books from one to the other, in the translation's order
#   *          every book
#   =nt        the books of another group
#   -member    takes those books away again
#
# A book the translation doesn't have is left out. A group's name may be
# shortened in a search to as many letters as make it unique ("=n", "=go").
#
# These are for every translation. groups.NAME (such as groups.KJVA), or
# "groups" in a translation's folder, replaces any of them for one
# translation whose publisher arranges its books differently.

ot              * -=nt          # the Old Testament: all but the New,
                                # as each translation arranges its books
nt              mat..rev        # the New Testament

law             gen exo lev num deu
history         jos judg ruth 1sa 2sa 1ki 2ki 1ch 2ch ezr neh est
poetry          job psa pro ecc son
majorprophets   isai jer lam eze dan
minorprophets   hos joe amo oba jon mic nah hab zep hag zec mal

gospels         mat mar luk joh
synoptics       mat mar luk
paul            rom..phile      # Romans to Philemon
pastoral        1ti 2ti tit
general         jam..jude       # James to Jude
john            joh 1jo 2jo 3jo rev
